[h3]Less Thermometer-Watching, More Delivering[/h3]

Temperature limits have been given a much smaller clipboard.

[list]
[*] Large, busy colonies should feel smoother when lots of buildings use delivery temperature limits. The mod now keeps track of the materials and destinations that actually need checking instead of repeatedly taking the temperature of the whole colony.
[*] Delivery decisions and temperature-aware “Lacks Resources” warnings should remain more responsive as colonies grow, while continuing to respect the limits you set.
[*] The same improvements apply to both the base game and [i]Spaced Out![/i], including colonies spread across multiple asteroids and storage aboard rockets.
[*] Existing temperature limits, construction settings, copied settings, and side-screen controls continue to work as before. The filing cabinet survived the renovation.
[*] Added best-efforts compatibility with Fast Track 0.18.4 when it is enabled. Colonies without Fast Track stay on the normal game route and do not carry any compatibility luggage.
[/list]

Every colony is its own lovingly overcomplicated thermodynamic incident, so results will vary. No Duplicants were asked to benchmark molten tungsten.
